  "decision_reason": "The ordinary inline hint does not remove the additional coordinate helper: assembly retains a 197-byte helper and 78-byte Point2 wrapper, versus the original 340-byte Point2 implementation. Rational medians improve by 60\u201379%, while symbolic rows remain mixed and query-only aggregate medians are 217.682 versus 222.578 ms. All exact witnesses and 21 focused tests match, but this is not an admitted production optimization.",
  "next_step": "Evaluate an explicit inline(always) on the private helper to remove the observed call layer, verify emitted code, and repeat the same costs. Tests and documentation now use only established production APIs, ready for isolated validation if costs support continuing.",
  "limitations": "Five fresh processes per version and mode, CPU 0, alternating order. No counting allocator in timing binaries; memory counts requested Rust bytes and excludes allocator metadata/native heaps. Eight point families, including shared-handle and copied-coordinate controls. First is a new pair, not empty global caches. Construction and explicit numerical preparation are measured separately. This scalar/point early gate does not admit full application behavior or production source.",
